{
  "requirement": "TBV automatically redacts recognized credentials in source excerpts delivered\nby its inspection tools and in node text supplied to its agent requests.\nThe built-in rules replace recognized secret regions with redaction markers\nwhile preserving line breaks. SDK-supplied outline languages use the same redacted\nregions, so changing only a recognized credential does not change its\nstructural fingerprint.\n\nLoaded source snapshots retain the original text for selection and spans;\nredaction applies when preparing model-visible text and structural hashes.\nFilesystem evidence storage preserves the supplied record. Applications supply\ntheir own answer values and remain responsible for what those answers contain.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.sdk.sources.redaction`. I found no test-adequacy gap.\n\n**1. Redaction in source excerpts from inspection tools**\n- `search_excerpts_redact_credentials_before_serialization_and_paging` in `project_sources.rs` drives the production tool dispatcher, `Session::dispatch`, for `search_text` and `search_structure`.\n- The source contains a GitHub token and a multi-line RSA private key. The test asserts the exact redacted excerpt, with surrounding code preserved.\n- It asserts the line count is unchanged, the token and key body lines are absent from the serialized output, and the match is not split across pages.\n- It checks that the dependency recorded by `finish_search` carries the fingerprint of the original snapshot.\n- It checks that the file on disk is unchanged.\n- The other source-delivery path, `SourceTools` in `agent/sources.rs`, is `#[cfg(test)]`-only (confirmed through its wrapper in `agent.rs`). It is not a production inspection surface, so it needs no redaction test.\n\n**2. Redaction in node text supplied to agent requests**\n- `queued_contents_and_graph_read_tools_redact_credentials_before_delivery` in `agent/tests.rs` covers both the queued `contents_of_current_node` path and the `read_node` tool.\n- For every request, it asserts the serialized chat history does not contain the credential and does contain the redaction marker.\n- It also asserts the recorded dependency fingerprint and the stored graph contents equal the original text.\n\n**3. Built-in rules, markers and line breaks**\n- `private_keys_are_redacted_from_header_through_body_keeping_lines` checks the private-key region and exact marker output. It checks line-count preservation in plain text and in Rust.\n- `tokens_in_code_are_redacted_without_adjacent_code` checks that adjacent code is untouched.\n- `regions_extend_both_ways_keep_crlf_and_scan_past_a_mebibyte` covers CRLF preservation, region extension and chaining, and a scan past 1 MiB.\n- `slices_concatenate_to_the_redacted_whole` checks that slices of adjacent ranges concatenate to the whole redacted text at every split point.\n- `heuristic_findings_alone_are_not_redacted` and `configuration_keys_do_not_add_sdk_specific_secret_rules` check that only recognized credentials are redacted. Plain config keys and high-entropy values alone are not.\n\n**4. Outline languages share the redacted regions**\n- `hashes_do_not_depend_on_credential_values` shows structural hashes are equal when only the credential changes. It covers Rust, Markdown and plain text. It also asserts that a change outside the redacted region still changes the hash.\n- `redaction_never_changes_an_outline` shows the outline structure is identical with and without redaction. It covers YAML, Rust, TOML, Markdown and text. It also shows that parsing the redacted YAML text itself would change the structure, which is why the original is parsed.\n\n**5. Snapshots retain the original text**\n- `formatted_contents_redact_credentials_while_retaining_raw_text_and_spans` asserts `text()` equals the original and `format()` is redacted.\n- It asserts that changing only the token leaves the fingerprint unchanged.\n- It asserts that a selected node's `text()` keeps the token while its `format()` redacts it.\n\n**6. Filesystem storage preserves the supplied record**\n- `storage_preserves_completed_answers_containing_credential_shaped_text` stores and loads an answer containing a token-shaped value. It asserts the loaded output is equal and the raw stored file contains the token.\n\n**7. Applications supply their own answers**\n- This clause is a statement of responsibility and states no testable behavior.\n\nNo {fixme} acknowledgments apply.",
  "references": "bd6b2738ddefb950bba56fda9c12fc5c2ff07ea9457dd6ccdaff4a64d36d0017",
